  "findings": {
    "Man_Elder": "Study07 frontal2400 still exposes orange skin, clear atframe60 (small patch also54). Right view reveals severely thinned/open-looking2400 legs and skin through robe at8000 across sampled phases. Rear and side show jagged/layered garment intersections. Frontal improvements do not establish clearance.",
    "Woman_Young": "Study07 retains trim better, but2400 right-view legs are severely thinned/open-looking, and skirt shading and layered intersections remain.8000 closer to source but skirt and layer changes still visible. Rear source already has a dark neckline/head-covering edge; do not label that whole feature a new candidate defect.",
    "baselineComparison": "Study03 right views already show robe skin exposure, folds/shading and jagged hems. Its2400 legs keep much more silhouette than Study07. Thus07 color preservation trades away geometry quality, particularly legs. Neither is adopted.",
    "nextAction": "Measure triangle distribution and protect limb volume plus layered garment clearance. Investigate per-part/material budgets or source topology reduction rather than escalating global color weighting."
  },
